### Approved separation and supported triggers
tickets/in-progress/explicit-agent-provider-composition-and-scope-assembly/requirements.md:9:Make provider construction and Agent Tools MCP capability issuance explicit at the two supported execution roots. Preserve the passed `ApplicationExecutionScope` and separate `GeneralProcessRunSupervisor`, while removing mixed-level provider dependencies, positional default/global selection, duplicated construction policy, and the scope's partial tuple-based kernel assembly.
tickets/in-progress/explicit-agent-provider-composition-and-scope-assembly/requirements.md:16:| BEH-002 | General and application roots independently construct AutoByteus, Codex, and Claude factories, including positional `undefined` values that select defaults. | Both roots call one immutable, named provider-factory builder with an exact definition service and execution-local session issuer. | General/application managers, sessions, task roots, cleanup, and mutable state remain non-identical. | REQ-003, REQ-004; AC-004, AC-005 |
tickets/in-progress/explicit-agent-provider-composition-and-scope-assembly/requirements.md:48:Adopt the clean-cut Host -> scoped Authority -> narrow Issuer -> issued descriptor boundary and one explicit provider-factory builder. Replace, rather than wrap, the old mixed-level manager/runtime shapes. Use a private scope-kernel builder for construction/unwind.
tickets/in-progress/explicit-agent-provider-composition-and-scope-assembly/requirements.md:58:- UC-001: Studio boot constructs one process MCP host, one general execution family, and one application scope.
tickets/in-progress/explicit-agent-provider-composition-and-scope-assembly/requirements.md:59:- UC-002: standalone boot constructs the same ownership pattern for the selected application.
tickets/in-progress/explicit-agent-provider-composition-and-scope-assembly/requirements.md:60:- UC-003: AutoByteus/Codex/Claude Agent create or restore receives the exact execution-local MCP issuer.
tickets/in-progress/explicit-agent-provider-composition-and-scope-assembly/requirements.md:61:- UC-004: post-issuance provider preparation failure immediately revokes the claimed run's sessions.
tickets/in-progress/explicit-agent-provider-composition-and-scope-assembly/requirements.md:69:- Repository-wide removal of provider-local defaults used by unrelated low-level/test construction. Supported server roots are governed instead.
tickets/in-progress/explicit-agent-provider-composition-and-scope-assembly/requirements.md:73:BEH-001–BEH-006 are fixed. In particular, general and application execution remain separate, RootTeamRun-local delegation stays unchanged, application/public definitions remain canonical, and all passed Studio/standalone execution, publication, streaming, recovery, reentry, nested-Team, and shutdown behavior remains valid.
tickets/in-progress/explicit-agent-provider-composition-and-scope-assembly/requirements.md:86:- **REQ-004:** Each builder call shall create fresh backend factories and execution-local provider session state while explicitly reusing only named process-owned immutable dependencies. The two execution families shall remain non-identical.
tickets/in-progress/explicit-agent-provider-composition-and-scope-assembly/requirements.md:97:- **AC-004:** Both roots receive the same provider builder identity; two builder calls return non-identical backend factories and bind them to the exact supplied issuer and definition service.
